{
  "summary": "This experiment tested the simplest multimodal extension of the best RNA-only configuration by adding ResNet50 image features via concat fusion to the scvi_n200 multiprofile avgpool pipeline, yielding a validation accuracy of 0.632 (F1 0.607) versus 0.650 (F1 0.628) for the RNA-only baseline (llm_summary_004). Because only the image channel and concat fusion were introduced relative to that baseline, this single-variable comparison indicates that, under this specific configuration, the ResNet50 image features do not provide complementary discriminative signal and instead slightly degrade performance by approximately 1.9 accuracy points. It remains uncertain whether alternative fusion strategies (e.g., gated or attention-based), different image encoders, or adjusted image preprocessing could recover meaningful multimodal gains, or whether the RNA-only multiprofile pipeline is already near the achievable ceiling for this task."
}

